  "notes": [
    "-AR verb with accent shift: the *i* carries a written accent in all stressed forms (yo/tú/él/ellos in presente and subjuntivo presente), but not in nosotros/nosotras where stress falls on the ending",
    "Same pattern as *enviar* → *envío*, *guiar* → *guío*",
    "Past participle: *confiado*",
    "*confiar en alguien/algo* = to trust someone/something (*Confío en ti* — I trust you)",
    "*confiar en + infinitive* = to be confident that (*Confío en ganar* — I'm confident of winning)",
    "*confiarle algo a alguien* = to entrust something to someone (*Le confié el secreto* — I confided the secret to him)",
    "*confiado/a* (adjective) = trusting, confident, overconfident"
  ],
